    estimatedMinutes: 12,
    prompt: "A graph is bipartite when its vertices split into two groups with every edge crossing between them. Colour neighbours oppositely; an edge joining two same-coloured vertices is a contradiction.\n\nReturn `True` if the **undirected** graph is bipartite. Check every component — the graph may be disconnected.\n\nA triangle is not bipartite; a 4-cycle is.",
