    difficulty: { concept: 5, implementation: 5, recall: 5 },
    estimatedMinutes: 16,
    prompt: "A **bridge** is an edge whose removal disconnects the graph. Low-link records the oldest discovery time reachable from a subtree; when a child's low-link is greater than its parent's discovery time, nothing in that subtree can get back around, so the edge is a bridge.\n\nReturn the bridges of an undirected graph as a sorted list of `(min, max)` pairs.\n\n`(3, [(0, 1), (1, 2)])` gives `[(0, 1), (1, 2)]`; a triangle has none.",
    exportName: "find_bridges",
    scaffolds: { L1: "def find_bridges(vertex_count, edges):\n    pass", L2: "def find_bridges(vertex_count, edges):\n    pass", L3: "def find_bridges(vertex_count, edges):\n    pass", L4: "" },
    tests: [
      { name: "every path edge is a bridge", code: "assert fn(3, [(0, 1), (1, 2)]) == [(0, 1), (1, 2)]", hidden: false },
      { name: "a cycle has no bridges", code: "assert fn(3, [(0, 1), (1, 2), (2, 0)]) == []", hidden: false },
      { name: "cycle plus a tail", code: "assert fn(4, [(0, 1), (1, 2), (2, 0), (2, 3)]) == [(2, 3)]", hidden: false },
      { name: "no edges", code: "assert fn(3, []) == []", hidden: false },
      { name: "parallel edges are not bridges", code: "assert fn(2, [(0, 1), (0, 1)]) == []", hidden: true }
    ],
    hints: [
      { rung: 0, text: "Skip the specific edge you arrived on, by index — not merely the parent vertex." },
      { rung: 1, text: "Low-link starts at the discovery time and shrinks toward anything reachable below." },
      { rung: 2, text: "A child whose low-link exceeds this vertex's discovery time hangs off a bridge." }
    ],
    solution: "def find_bridges(vertex_count, edges):\n    adjacency = [[] for _ in range(vertex_count)]\n    for index, (left, right) in enumerate(edges):\n        adjacency[left].append((right, index))\n        adjacency[right].append((left, index))\n    discovery = [-1] * vertex_count\n    low = [0] * vertex_count\n    bridges = []\n    timer = [0]\n    def visit(vertex, via):\n        discovery[vertex] = low[vertex] = timer[0]\n        timer[0] += 1\n        for neighbour, index in adjacency[vertex]:\n            if index == via:\n                continue\n            if discovery[neighbour] == -1:\n                visit(neighbour, index)\n                low[vertex] = min(low[vertex], low[neighbour])\n                if low[neighbour] > discovery[vertex]:\n                    bridges.append((min(vertex, neighbour), max(vertex, neighbour)))\n            else:\n                low[vertex] = min(low[vertex], discovery[neighbour])\n    for start in range(vertex_count):\n        if discovery[start] == -1:\n            visit(start, -1)\n    return sorted(bridges)",
